Description: a plain read of an image the stereo layer did not make a pair is not announced as a pair (ORDER 581)
 A marked picture (a PNG with an sTER chunk, or any file whose reader reports its own stereo mark) set to "Not 3D" in the
 shared per-file store gets a pair thumbnail in Dolphin: the layer's loadPair() answers "not a pair", the image
 thumbnailer reads the file plainly, the edition's Qt (and KImageFormats' readers) put the file's own Stereo3DLayout text
 on that image, and the thumbnail worker (thumbnail.cpp, stereoLayout()) sends it as stereo3dLayout and the job caches it
 as X-KDE::Stereo3DLayout. The text is cleared on the image the layer did not make a pair. The JPEG thumbnailer reads with
 the plain JPEG reader (QImageReader(path, "jpeg")), which reports no such text, and needs no change.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-15
---
--- a/thumbnail/imagecreator.cpp
+++ b/thumbnail/imagecreator.cpp
@@ -94,6 +94,13 @@
     ir.read(&img);
 
     if (!img.isNull()) {
+#if HAVE_STEREO_LAYER
+        // The stereo layer decided above that this file is not a pair (the person's "Not 3D" for it, or a view of one eye,
+        // or no pair at all), so the reader's own stereo mark (the edition's Qt reports a PNG's sTER chunk, and
+        // KImageFormats' readers theirs, as the text Stereo3DLayout) must not reach the thumbnail worker, which announces
+        // and caches any such text as a pair
+        img.setText(QStringLiteral("Stereo3DLayout"), QString());
+#endif
         return KIO::ThumbnailResult::pass(img);
     }
 
